# Cloudflare Pages response headers (QA F65).
# Every page: nosniff, a strict referrer and no camera / microphone / location / payment.
# Each page also gets its own Content-Security-Policy in the generated block below: inline scripts run only if their SHA-256 hash is
# listed, no inline handlers, connections only to the shipped workers (and loopback for local mocks). The staff dashboard (approve /
# retract buttons, staff token in localStorage) can never be framed (clickjacking).
# Pages joins the values of a header set by two matching rules with a comma (two policies, both enforced), so no CSP goes on /*.
# After editing an inline script: `cargo run -q -p pages-csp` and commit this file. CI and deploy_pages.sh run `--check`.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

